@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2200 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [499 x i8] }> <{ [499 x i8] c"The kind of citation to produce. Different forms are useful in different\0Ascenarios: A normal citation is useful as a source at the end of a\0Asentence, while a \22prose\22 citation is more suitable for inclusion in the\0Aflow of text.\0A\0AIf set to `{none}`, the cited work is included in the bibliography, but\0Anothing will be displayed.\0A\0A```example\0A#cite(<netwok>, form: \22prose\22)\0Ashow the outsized effects of\0Apirate life on the human psyche.\0A>>> #set text(0pt)\0A>>> #bibliography(\22works.bib\22, style: \22apa\22)\0A```" }>, align 1
@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2201 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [351 x i8] }> <{ [351 x i8] c"The citation style.\0A\0AShould be either `{auto}`, one of the built-in styles (see below) or a\0Apath to a [CSL file](https://citationstyles.org/). Some of the styles\0Alisted below appear twice, once with their full name and once with a\0Ashort alias.\0A\0AWhen set to `{auto}`, automatically use the\0A[bibliography's style]($bibliography.style) for the citations." }>, align 1
